-- title:
--   König's lemma for feasible nodes
-- statement:
--   In an ordered tree, let a node $v$ at level $n$ be feasible if some witness $d$ in a fixed set $B$ satisfies $f_i(\mathrm{anc}_i(v),d)\ge\frac12$ for all $0<i\le n$. If every level contains a feasible node, there is a branch $b_0,b_1,\dots$ (each $b_i$ an ancestor of $b_j$ for $i\le j$) with
--   $$
--   b_n\ \text{feasible for every }n .
--   $$
--
--   Finitely many nodes per level and feasibility closed under ancestors give an infinite feasible path.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Nonexpansive/FeasibleBranch.lean#L71-L98

